Before the prompts themselves, a setup note that should help quality across the batch.

## Shared world preamble

You can prepend this to any of the prompts below. Keeps the visual continuity tight — same planet, same water, same lighting register — and saves you re-typing the setting every time.

```
[SETTING] An aquatic alien organism from Cassiopeia-3b, a tectonically young
ocean world with a sulfuric sea at pH 3.8. Murky greenish-yellow water,
dense with sulfur particulate and copper salts in suspension. Bioluminescent
plankton in the background. Volumetric god-rays from a dim red dwarf star
filtering through acidic haze above. Hydrothermal vent silhouettes in the
distance. Chemosynthetic ecosystem, no calcium carbonate present anywhere.
[STYLE] Scientific specimen photography meets concept art, naturalistic
proportions, biologically plausible, David Attenborough documentary still,
shot on cinema camera, shallow depth of field, dramatic underwater lighting,
photorealistic textures, 8k detail.
```

For each creature below, append the creature-specific description. I'll keep them dense with concrete visual nouns — txt2img models do better with "translucent gelatinous bell with internal copper veining" than with "majestic" or "fearsome."

